WEBVTT

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:53.230
Joe, you did well.

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:54.610
Joe, you did well.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:58.900
Hey! Old man!

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:00.170
Hey!

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:01.550
We're home, old man!

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:03.630
Oh, so everyone's shown up!

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:04.990
You're home early today, Nishi!

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:08.000
Yeah. Old Hayashi wanted me to go look after Joe,

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.820
so he let me out early.

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:11.400
I see.

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:16.700
So, how's Joe doing?

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.940
I came here to get engaged to Joe!

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:21.160
No, we only came to visit him, stupid!

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.570
Did that scruffy doctor from over there drop by today?

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:28.370
What was the diagnosis? What was the scruffy doctor's diagnosis?

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:30.940
Yeah, he may be a little scruffy...

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.080
He said there's nothing wrong with him...

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:37.600
but anyway, as long as Joe takes it easy, he'll be up and about by tomorrow!

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:39.390
That's great news!

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.390
Thank goodness!

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.390
<i>Hooray! Bro Joe's all right!</i>

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:45.470
Yippee! I'm so happy!

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:48.480
But he's lucky he's even able to stand.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:51.190
Joe keeps getting beat up every match.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:52.980
If that continues, he'll be crippled.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.490
B-Beat up? C-Crippled?

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:56.490
<i>No way!</i>

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.170
But more importantly, old man,

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:02.920
we should worry about getting Joe fighting fit again as soon as possible!

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:04.840
Oh, that's right!

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:08.000
I got a whole load of food to help Joe recover his stamina!

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:10.040
Recover his stamina?

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:12.540
Give me that.

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:25.690
That's good... That too...

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:34.280
Everything else would just spell temptation!

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:44.620
Wh-What do you think you're doing, old man?

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.620
Have you gone mad?

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:50.120
Mammoth spent his own money on all that!

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:53.070
Boxers who are just starting out don't make that much!

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:54.970
You just wasted his hard-earned money!

00:03:54.970 --> 00:03:56.630
You're wrong, old man!

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.360
Hush up!

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:03.090
Even without all that stuff, Joe's been gaining weight from resting up for six days!

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:05.890
But you didn't have to toss it all into the drainage ditch—

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:06.600
Nishi,

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:08.580
you're a fledgling pro boxer.

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:11.280
You should know the difference between what's good to eat and what's not!

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:14.510
When a boxer's healing up, he should eat just enough to provide nutrition...

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:16.110
and then rest up peacefully!

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.130
So, stay out of it!

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:18.610
Besides,

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:22.200
your match is coming up soon.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.890
If you don't watch what you eat,

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:26.660
you'll have to worry about your weight again!

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:39.670
Damn! The old man's so cold!

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:42.780
He didn't have to throw it into the drainage canal!

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:43.680
Dammit!

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:44.170
You said it!

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:46.090
I thought he was better than that!

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:47.870
Yeah! We could have eaten them!

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.180
What a waste.

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:54.690
Well, I'm off to work.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:56.490
Old man... Don't you usually work during the day?

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:58.190
Old man... Don't you usually work during the day?

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:04.150
It's not like when we didn't have a license. We've got fight money rolling in now.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:08.680
And we've still got our jobs at Hayashi-san's.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:10.700
You don't have to work at night too.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.290
Don't you worry about me.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:14.580
Be sure to make Joe's dinner at six.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:17.910
And don't make too much, even if he says he wants more.

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:18.710
Yes.

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:20.830
Goodbye!

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:21.670
And good riddance!

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:28.020
Old man...

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:29.660
Why...

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:31.180
Why are you so cold?

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:47.280
Is Bro Joe asleep?

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:52.030
It's really quiet up there...

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:59.320
Hey, Mammoth, can we check on him?

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:01.670
Okay, if you're quiet!

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:03.960
I know, I know!

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:13.250
What's all the noise about? Can't you leave a man in peace!?

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.250
It's Bro Joe!

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:17.270
There he is!

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:17.270
<i>You're right!</i>

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:19.910
Seriously, I can't sleep.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:21.940
I'm hungry!

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:24.860
Bro Joe!

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:26.140
It's Bro Joe!

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:27.370
I'll take care of you kids later.

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:28.870
Hey, Nishi! Is dinner ready yet?

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:31.870
Joe, you should be resting!

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:34.740
Don't treat me like I'm dying! These are just scratches!

00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:37.380
Hey, where's the old man?

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.870
He went to work his night job.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:45.030
Well, good on him. Now, let's see here...

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:47.840
I'm starting to go soft. Better start my training!

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:55.620
J-Joe! Don't push yourself!

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:01.200
Special delivery for Tange-san.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:02.260
Oh, thank you!

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:04.150
A special delivery at this hour?

00:07:05.510 --> 00:07:07.630
I don't know what it is, but that sounded urgent!

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:10.560
I'm gonna go take it to the old man!

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:13.160
Don't panic. First off, read it and find out what it's about.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:15.100
Oh, good idea.

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:20.810
Let's see: "We have accepted your application."

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:27.490
"Leaving the money aside, we will have a van awaiting you first thing on the 31st."

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:28.170
I see...

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:29.220
What?

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:31.510
Gimme that!

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:36.700
Uchiyama Kan'emon from Sarusuberi Village in Gunma Prefecture.

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:37.980
You know the guy, Nishi?

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:39.260
No.

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:41.610
But forget that, Joe. The 31st is tomorrow!

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:44.480
He said he'd be waiting for us. What is the meaning of this postcard?

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:50.240
Joe, what's going on?

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:51.490
Come with me, Nishi!

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:54.600
Y-You kids hold the fort for us!

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:03.500
Kinoko! Hyoromatsu!

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:04.970
Yes!

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:05.920
Roger...

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:07.460
...that!

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:17.060
So? What's this all about, old man?

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:18.870
Tell us what's going on!

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:25.830
Don't tell me that even though you got a license for the gym,

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:29.680
you're still gonna be forced to trade us or have someone else take over.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:31.450
Well? Tell us, old man!

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:35.450
They finally replied. I was about to give up hope.

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:39.760
Stop muttering to yourself and explain!

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:42.410
What does it mean when it says our application's been accepted?

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:49.960
Wh-What's so funny?

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:53.010
Look at the return address on the postcard again!

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:56.540
Sarusuberi Village in Gunma is a very famous place!

00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:58.510
It's a famous hot spring at the base of Mt. Akagi,

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:05.280
and legend has it that Kunisada Chuji himself went there to recover from a sword wound.

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:09.110
There's no way there'd be a boxing gym that deep in the mountains.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:13.490
There's a guy over there who used 
to be my backer during my boxing days.

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:15.990
So, who's this Uchiyama Kan'emon?

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:18.770
Oh him. He's the manager of the hot springs.

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:20.950
Now, let me explain...

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:24.040
Although I take pride in how I run my gym,

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:29.070
I still regret not having done anything nice for you two.

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:33.620
But I figured we could go on a trip to the hot springs over the New Year to make up for it.

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:38.620
I asked Mr. Uchiyama to give me a discount for old time's sake.

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:40.970
I-Is that true, old man?

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:45.980
So, you were working nights to save up the money for it?

00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:48.800
Well, that's the problem with running a gym steeped in poverty!

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:52.300
This is great!

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:55.490
Hear that, Nishi? We can go skiing!

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:58.730
Now that you know, go home and rest!

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:02.210
Tomorrow, we're going to the hot springs to help Joe recuperate and help Nishi lose weight!

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:04.950
O-Old man, I'm...

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:07.660
What's the matter, Nishi?

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:12.750
I said all these horrible things about you... that you had a heart of stone...

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:15.120
I'm sorry! Please accept my apology!

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:19.270
Forget about it!

00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:22.010
I was hoping to surprise you!

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:23.980
But I probably shouldn't have kept it a secret.

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:26.450
Old man. Thank you. Thank you so much...

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:32.990
D-Don't kowtow to me, idiot! This isn't a samurai movie!

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:35.500
Seriously, what the hell is going on?

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:39.780
Anyway, let's start packing as soon as we're back at the gym! Yeah, let's go!

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:41.280
I can go skiing!

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:11.530
Now, lessee, this one here...

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:14.390
Is this the place?

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:20.330
Hi, thank you for coming!

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:22.120
Yes, we're on our way!

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:24.310
Hey, stop dawdling! We're heading out!

00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:26.290
What's the rush?

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:27.620
We need to close the place up...

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:28.370
I've already done that!

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:32.240
If we waste time here and those kids catch on, we'll be in trouble!

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:33.560
Now, hurry!

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:39.170
Good morning!

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:40.940
Y-You kids... How did you...?

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:42.160
Y-You kids... How did you...?

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:46.460
 Good morning!

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:51.140
Mr. Danpei, you truly are a great man. I'm so happy you're taking us slum folk to the hot springs.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:53.650
Hear, hear!

00:11:55.910 --> 00:11:57.910
You little brats!

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:01.810
There was something wrong with us yesterday...

00:12:01.810 --> 00:12:06.040
We didn't mean to badmouth a man as nice as Mr. Danpei!

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:09.890
Yeah! We realized that we just weren't good judges of character,

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:12.210
and we spent all night repenting. Isn't that right?

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:12.920
Right!

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:15.420
Hear, hear!

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:18.900
Enough of your cheerleading!

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:20.920
This is why I told you to hurry!

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:23.880
If it's all the same with you, I'd like to hit the road!

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:27.990
Hip, hip, hooray!

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:44.620
How many more sleeps until New Year's?

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:44.620
<i>Hey, hey!</i>

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:52.010
How many more sleeps until New Year's?

00:12:52.010 --> 00:12:57.770
How many more sleeps until New Year's?

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:54.960
<i>What a racket!</i>

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:57.770
<i>Hey, pipe down!</i>

00:13:00.930 --> 00:13:04.200
According to the doctor's statement, after a lengthy diagnosis,

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:08.490
it's been confirmed that boxer Wolf Kanagushi has broken his jaw in several places,

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:13.660
ruling out any hope of a comeback.

00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:15.520
Now, onto our next item.

00:13:17.470 --> 00:13:18.520
Wolf...

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:21.650
Wolf can't recover from his injuries? The very same Wolf?

00:13:31.300 --> 00:13:34.640
Driver, can you turn right at the next street?

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:38.490
But I have to go straight to get on the highway!

00:13:38.490 --> 00:13:41.170
There's somewhere I'd like to stop first.

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.720
Old man, where are we going?

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:48.680
I don't want to get Joe all 
depressed while he's still recovering,

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:52.000
but this is the duty of a boxer.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:55.800
We're going to Asia Gym to talk to Coach Otaka about Wolf.

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:56.690
Aren't we, Joe?

00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:58.120
Yeah.

00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:00.770
Fine by me.

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:17.460
And so, we came right as soon as we heard the news.

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:20.170
Um... What can we say? Uh...

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:23.860
I wish I could tell you that this is a kind gesture of yours,

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:27.180
but, in all honesty, your presence here is a nuisance.

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:28.500
Otaka-kun, I know this is hard for you...

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:30.540
Otaka-kun, I know this is hard for you...

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:35.730
But even Joe came here to pay his respects while he's still recovering!

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:39.150
We really are here to express our sympathy for you...

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:45.150
Don't get the wrong idea. I'm not hung up on Wolf not being able to recover.

00:14:46.430 --> 00:14:47.150
What do you mean?

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:49.710
He was even called the King of the Rookies!

00:14:49.710 --> 00:14:53.910
To think that some oddball novice would be the one to put him out of action...

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:57.250
Now that's what I call a laughingstock!

00:14:57.250 --> 00:15:00.710
If you think about it, he's brought shame on Asia Gym.

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:03.620
That's why I want to forget about that good-for-nothing Wolf

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:06.380
as soon as humanly possible.

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:08.590
Otaka-kun, you're such a-

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:11.350
That means Wolf has nothing now!

00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:14.950
He fought for you and Asia Gym!

00:15:14.950 --> 00:15:18.730
You'd pet his head if he won, and kick him like a dog if he lost?

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:20.520
That kind of fucked-up way of thinking

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:22.150
is unacceptable!

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:22.850
You got that?

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:26.950
Well, I have to go now.

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:28.860
We'll meet again.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:30.510
Are you running away, you son of a—

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:31.440
Joe!

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:36.750
So, Otaka-kun, now Wolf's out for good, you're gonna find a way for him to support himself, right?

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:41.080
Beats me. He'll have to figure that out himself.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.080
Hey! Get back here!

00:15:43.970 --> 00:15:46.390
They're sure taking their time...

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:50.120
I'm so bored and hungry...

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:52.900
It's a little early, but why don't we get out our lunches?

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:54.470
Yeah, let's do it!

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:57.520
Thanks for the food!

00:15:57.520 --> 00:15:58.770
Thanks for the food!

00:15:58.770 --> 00:15:59.330
Wait!

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:00.920
H-Hey, look!

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:04.340
Wait, Otaka-kun!

00:16:04.340 --> 00:16:06.300
That's not fair on Wolf!

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:09.430
He at least needs a way to support himself...

00:16:09.430 --> 00:16:10.530
Shut up!

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:11.770
Let me go!

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:13.280
Dammit...

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:15.150
You piece of shit!

00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:16.480
What are you trying to do!?

00:16:17.800 --> 00:16:20.290
Hey! Somebody, help!

00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:22.210
You asshole!

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:03.290
Help me!

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:15.600
That felt good!

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:17.760
Serves him right!

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:20.900
But I'm really hungry now...

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:23.730
We really should've saved a rice ball or two...

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:42.720
I'm so hungry, I'm so hungry, I'm so hungry...

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:19.190
Wolf!

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:39.220
Wolf...

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:41.470
Joe.

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:46.900
You still awake, old man?

00:18:48.220 --> 00:18:51.400
Joe, don't let Wolf's fate get you down.

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:55.070
That's just the way boxing is sometimes.

00:18:57.090 --> 00:19:00.270
You can't waste your energy worrying about Wolf.

00:19:01.220 --> 00:19:03.760
When your tomorrow comes, Rikiishi will...

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:06.860
A great man called Rikiishi will be waiting for you!

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:08.410
Yeah. I know, old man.

00:19:39.020 --> 00:19:41.850
Oh, Joe! You're here already?

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:48.080
What a great view...

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:49.830
Yeah.

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:56.590
The snow sure is pretty...

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:05.430
So this is where you've been hiding!

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:17.330
The water's so nice... The water's so nice...

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:19.090
<i>Oh! There you are!</i>

00:20:17.330 --> 00:20:23.490
This is the Joshu spring of Sarusuberi...

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:31.630
The water's so nice... The water's so nice...

00:20:31.630 --> 00:20:38.610
This is the Joshu spring of Sarusuberi...

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:47.640
Take that!

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:49.140
Go!

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:54.190
Now you've done it!

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:58.870
Here! Payback time!

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:03.190
Have a taste of this!

00:21:09.190 --> 00:21:16.700
So, winter has come to the hot springs resort?{do we have separate style for singing?}

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:27.760
The snow has fallen, fallen, and underwear! Clap, clap, get out the rice bowl, underwear! Clap, clap...

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:29.590
Why, thank you...

00:21:33.380 --> 00:21:34.650
It's good!

00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:39.370
This is great!

00:23:15.950 --> 00:23:18.430
The fight with Wolf is over.

00:23:18.430 --> 00:23:22.090
Joe is now doing all he can to move on toward tomorrow.

00:23:22.660 --> 00:23:27.130
The man who ignited Joe's wild instincts in juvie...

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:27.920
Rikiishi Toru...

00:23:28.910 --> 00:23:33.680
Rikiishi is the reason that Joe is now a boxer.

00:23:33.680 --> 00:23:39.290
That's why they now live in a world where they can't avoid each other.

00:23:39.290 --> 00:23:43.440
But if Joe and Rikiishi fight, one of them is bound to get hurt...

00:23:44.130 --> 00:23:47.020
Even so, Joe and Rikiishi dare to fight each other!

00:23:47.710 --> 00:23:51.950
This match is likely to be a bloody one!

00:23:52.720 --> 00:23:58.540
Now, Rikiishi has begun a hellish weight-loss regimen in order to match up with Joe.

00:23:58.540 --> 00:24:02.130
Now, for Joe, as he accepts Rikiishi's challenge...

00:24:02.130 --> 00:24:04.050
which way is tomorrow!?
